Annex 4 to the  
Policy and procedures for room 
allocation and accommodation in 
dormitories of the autonomous 
organization of education 
Nazarbayev University  

Rights and responsibilities of the resident assistant 

 The resident assistant has the right to:   
1) Inspect rooms within the assigned block to ensure that students comply with 
the Policy and Procedures. For this purpose, the resident assistant may collect and 
maintain information about the students residing in the assigned block;   
2) Submit proposals to the DSS for improving educational efforts, ensuring 
compliance with the Policy and Procedures, and enhancing students' living conditions in 
the dormitory;  
3) Make recommendations to the dormitory manager regarding the improvement 
of students' living conditions;      
4) Document violations of the Policy and Procedures and submit all related 
documents to the DSS; 
5) Submit requests to the Director of the DSS for the application of disciplinary 
measures against violators of the Policy and Procedures. 
The resident assistant is responsible for:  
1) Ensuring compliance with the Policy and Procedures and the Code of Conduct 
by students;  
2) Assisting in disseminating information to students regarding the Policy and 
Procedures, the Code of Conduct, and other accommodation-related matters, as directed 
by the DSS;  
3) Supporting the DSS in organizing and conducting educational and disciplinary 
activities with students; 
4) Immediately reporting emergency situations or any threats to the life and safety 
of students in the dormitory to DSS staff;  
5) Resolving conflicts between co -residing students and facilitating 
reconciliation, including assisting in the drafting of a roommate agreement if necessary; 
6) Maintaining composure and patience when communicating with resident 
students, University and Entity staff, and University guests; refraining from arguments, 
remaining self-controlled, and demonstrating respect for individuals of all races, 
nationalities, genders, religions, and other identities; 
7) Assisting Entity staff in evacuating resident students from the dormitory in 
case of a fire alarm and/or evacuation; 
8) Coordinating with the Entity to ensure students' compliance with the Policy 
and Procedures and the Code of Conduct;  
9) Planning activities within their scope of responsibility and submitting relevant 
reports to the DSS in accordance with Annex 6 to the Agreement; 
10)  Participating in training sessions related to the duties of a resident 
assistant;

